    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d168">

                <pb facs="0289" n="275" sameAs="frus:frus1949v05/pg275"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW
                    (Peace)/12–2249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in the United Kingdom
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-12-31T13:00:00-05:00">December 31,
                            1949—1 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4663. At meeting US, UK, Canada, Australia, New Zealand Reps Washn<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d168-f1"/> general agreement reached on Brit proposal Jan 5 as date
                        <pb facs="0290" n="276" xml:id="pg276"/> for delivery notes to Bulg, Hung,
                    Rum designating Treaty Commissioners (Embtel
                    5089, Dee 22<anchor n="2" xml:id="d168-f2"/>). Australia however has decided not
                    to name Commissioner at this stage preferring to await ICJ’s decisions on Questions I and II submitted by GA. New Zealand Rep said his Govt probably wld
                    refrain also but decision was not firm. Canada is proposing that Brit Mins in Hung and Rum deliver separate notes on
                    behalf Canada designating Justice J. L. Ilsley as Canadian Commissioner.</p>
                <p>Inform FonOff text proposed Brit notes shown
                    to Dept by Brit Emb here has our general concurrence. US Reps Hung, Bulg, Rum will
                    present parallel notes designating Dickinson Jan 5. US notes probably will refer
                    to previous notes of Aug 1 and Sep 19.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d168-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Tentatively agreed subj concurrence London and Ottawa to deliver copies of notes
                    to SYG through three UN Missions in New York at
                    11 AM Jan 6, with request to pass copies to members and ICJ. Text notes wld be released to press simultaneously in London,
                    Washn, Ottawa at 11:15 am, Washn time.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d168-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent London, rptd Canberra, and USUN, New
                        York.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d168-f5"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d168-f1" n="1" xml:id="d168-f1-content">
                <p>John C. Campbell’s memorandum of conversation covering the meeting under
                    reference here, held on December 28, is included in file 740.0011 EW (Peace)/12–2849.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d168-f2" n="2" xml:id="d168-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see footnote 3 to telegram 4486, December 15, to London, <ref
                        target="#pg275">p. 275</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d168-f3" n="3" xml:id="d168-f3-content">
                <p>Regarding the notes under reference here, see editorial notes, <ref
                        target="#pg260">pp. 260</ref> and <ref target="#pg264">264</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d168-f4" n="4" xml:id="d168-f4-content">
                <p>For the text of the note delivered by the Legation in Bucharest to the Romanian
                    Government on January 5, 1950, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, January 16, 1950, p. 97. The notes to the Bulgarian and
                    Hungarian Governments were substantially the same. See also the statement issued
                    to the press by the Department of State on January 6, 1950 regarding the naming
                    of Edwin D. Dickinson as Treaty Commissioner and the forwarding to the United
                    Nations Secretary General of recent exchanges of notes with the Balkan
                    Governments regarding the dispute over charges of violations of human rights
                    clauses of the peace treaties, <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, p. 97.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d168-f5" n="5" xml:id="d168-f5-content">
                <p>Repeated to Canberra as telegram 181 and to the United States Mission to United
                    Nations at New York as 664.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
